   "en_span": "chapters/epicurves.qmd:1341-1341",
   "tr_span": "chapters/epicurves.es.qmd:1305-1308",
   "proposition": "The English states that the easiest method for multi-level date labels is to pass scales::label_date_short() to the labels = argument of scale_x_date(), and that its labels adjust automatically as the data expand from days to weeks to months and years; the Spanish omits this method and its worked example entirely.",
   "reader_consequence": "A Spanish reader loses the simplest solution to the problem the section poses and is left only with the more elaborate faceting workaround, or hand-built \\n labels that do not adapt as the outbreak lengthens.",
